<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A31/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A31/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A31/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T09:49:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'thickness_of_stratiform_rainfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Amount" means mass per unit area.  The construction thickness_of_[X_]rainfall_amount means the accumulated "depth" of rainfall i.e. the thickness of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area as the rainfall amount.  Stratiform precipitation, whether liquid or frozen, is precipitation that formed in stratiform cloud.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV15A31'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A32/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A32/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A32/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T09:49:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'thickness_of_stratiform_snowfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Amount" means mass per unit area.  The construction thickness_of_[X_]snowfall_amount means the accumulated "depth" of snow which fell i.e. the thickness of the layer of snow at its own density. There are corresponding standard names for liquid water equivalent (lwe) thickness.  Stratiform precipitation, whether liquid or frozen, is precipitation that formed in stratiform cloud.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV15A32'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A6/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A6/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A6/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T09:49:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_stratiform_snowfall_rate'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Stratiform precipitation, whether liquid or frozen, is precipitation that formed in stratiform cloud.  "lwe" means liquid water equivalent.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV15A6'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A8/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A8/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A8/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T09:49:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_stratiform_snowfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Amount" means mass per unit area.  "lwe" means liquid water equivalent.  The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area.  Stratiform precipitation, whether liquid or frozen, is precipitation that formed in stratiform cloud.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV15A8'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N204/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N204/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N204/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T08:27:36'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'equivalent_reflectivity_factor'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Equivalent reflectivity factor"  is the radar reflectivity factor that is calculated from the measured radar return power assuming the target is composed of liquid water droplets whose diameter is less than one tenth of the radar wavelength, i.e., treating the droplets as Rayleigh scatterers.  The actual radar reflectivity factor would depend on the size distribution and composition of the particles within the target volume and these are  often unknown.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N204'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N57/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N57/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N57/>;
    dc:modified '2010-07-26T08:27:36'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sinking_mole_flux_of_aragonite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The phrase \'expressed_as\' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.   \'Sinking\' is the gravitational settling of particulate matter suspended in a liquid. A sinking flux is positive downwards and is calculated relative to the movement of the surrounding fluid. Aragonite is a mineral that is a polymorph of calcium carbonate. The chemical formula of aragonite is CaCO3. Standard names also exist for calcite, another polymorph of calcium carbonate.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF14N57'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N58/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N58/2/>
